<section class="container article-page"><div class="eyebrow">ADVENTURE GUIDE</div><h1>How to <em>Play</em></h1><p class="article-lead">Discover the dangers of the digital world across six different games, build safe habits and collect your points.</p>
<div class="rules-grid"><article><div class="rule-icon">🦊</div><h3>1. Create your hero</h3><p>Pick an avatar, choose a username and save your age range once.</p></article><article><div class="rule-icon">🎮</div><h3>2. Meet your game</h3><p>Start with any of the six games on your Player Dashboard.</p></article><article><div class="rule-icon">🎯</div><h3>3. Complete the missions</h3><p>Solve random tasks suited to your age range before time runs out.</p></article><article><div class="rule-icon">🏆</div><h3>4. Collect points</h3><p>You can earn up to 100 points in each game and 600 points in total.</p></article></div>
<div class="rule-wide"><h2>Game Rules</h2><ul><li>Do not use swear words, insults or inappropriate language in your username.</li><li>Do not impersonate anyone or use multiple accounts to game the leaderboard.</li><li>Never type your real password, verification codes or private information into the games.</li><li>You can enter each game up to 3 times. Games that time out or that you leave unfinished also count as an entry; your highest score goes on the leaderboard.</li><li>Don't forget to read the short safety explanations after your answers.</li><li>The games are for education; the messages and people shown are fictional.</li></ul></div>
<div class="rule-wide"><h2>Privacy and Participation</h2><p>Leaderboards show only your avatar and username. The first name, last name and email requested at sign-up are not public; only authorised admin roles can see them, for registration and contact purposes. Personal data should be processed only for the periods and purposes set by the event organiser. Real event registrations should not start until the required notices and legal steps for child participants are completed.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> This page does not replace a legal privacy notice. The organisation's data controller details and a notice under the applicable data protection law (e.g. GDPR/KVKK) must be published separately before going live.</p></div>
<div class="center-cta"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-xl" href="/register">Join the Adventure ➜</a></div></section>
